   "properties": {
    "id": "structure:murphy:well-9308",
    "name": "Well beside the grade (1954 map, 'Well 9308')",
    "valid_from": 1954,
    "valid_to": 1994,
    "grade": "measured",
    "error_ft": 40,
    "basis": "The 1954 Divide sheet marks a well, spot height 9308, beside the old railroad grade about 0.4 mile north of the mileage point (3.08 timetable miles from Divide); the 1994 sheet repeats it. The lidar ground there is 9,314 ft. What it served and when it was dug are not known; that it was the railway's or a stop's water supply is a conjecture with nothing to support it.",
